Problem statement

Given a Map<String, Integer>, find and return all keys whose corresponding values are null.

The solution should handle:
- An empty map.
- Multiple keys with null values.
- A map containing no null values.
- A map containing a null key.
- Different Map implementations such as HashMap and LinkedHashMap.


=========
1. Recommended solution – Java 8 Streams
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class NullValueKeys {

    public static List<String> findKeysWithNullValues(
            Map<String, Integer> map) {

        if (map == null || map.isEmpty()) {
            return Collections.emptyList();
        }

        return map.entrySet()
                .stream()
                .filter(entry -> entry.getValue() == null)
                .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Map<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

        map.put("Java", 100);
        map.put("Spring", null);
        map.put("Kafka", 200);
        map.put("Microservices", null);
        map.put("Docker", 300);

        List<String> result = findKeysWithNullValues(map);

        System.out.println(result);
    }
}

2. Alternative solutions
Approach 2: Traditional for-each loop
This is my preferred approach when readability, debugging and straightforward execution matter more than functional programming style.
public static List<String> findNullKeys(Map<String, Integer> map) {

    List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();

    if (map == null || map.isEmpty()) {
        return result;
    }

    for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : map.entrySet()) {
        if (entry.getValue() == null) {
            result.add(entry.getKey());
        }
    }

    return result;
}